title: Campaigning
new-page: true
on-arrival: month_actions += 1
max-visits: 36
is-card: true
card-image: img/flags.jpg
frequency: 100
tags: party_affairs

= Campaigning

Whether or not we are in an electoral campaign, the DDP is always looking to expand its voteshare. [? if ddp_votes < 6: However, our party has started to wander into moribund territory, and we must do something to stop the rapid fall of the [+ ddp_name +], or else we will become history. ?]

- @workers: The urban working class, who typically support the SPD.
- @new_middle: The "new middle class" of government employees and white-collar workers, our traditional voter base.
- @old_middle: The "old middle class" of small independent businessmen and artisans.
- @rural: Rural workers and small farmers, amongst who we are virtually unknown.
- @unemployed: The unemployed.
- @catholics: Catholics, who typically support the Z or the BVP.
- @root: We either don't want to or cannot campaign right now.
- @easy_discard

@workers
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: workers_ddp += 6*(1-dissent); workers_ddp -= 2 if unemployed >= 15; workers_ddp -= 2 if unemployed >= 25; workers_ddp += 6*(1-dissent); resources -= 1; workers_ddp += 3*(1-dissent); peoples_party_support += 1;

We have increased our campaigning among the workers, who typically support the SPD. [? if unemployed >= 15: The high levels of unemployment make our campaign more difficult. ?]

@new_middle
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: new_middle_ddp += 6*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd -= 4; resources -= 1;

We have increased our campaigning among the new middle class, the traditional voter base of the [+ ddp_name +], our party.

@old_middle
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: old_middle_ddp += 5*(1-dissent); resources -= 1;

We have increased our campaigning among the old middle class.

@rural
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: rural_ddp += 2*(1-dissent); rural_dnvp -= 2*(1-dissent); resources -= 1

We have increased our campaigning among farmers. The [+ ddp_name +] is unknown to many rural workers and landowners, so we have a harder time campaigning among these demographics.

@unemployed
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: unemployed_ddp += 6*(1-dissent); resources -= 1; unemployed_ddp -= 3 if welfare < 0; unemployed_ddp += 6*(1-dissent); unemployed_ddp += 3*(1-dissent) if welfare >= 2;

We have increased our campaigning among the unemployed. [? if welfare < 0: The welfare cuts and resultant poverty make our campaign more difficult, since we are associated with the government that enacted these cuts, and our campaign may even backfire. ?]

@catholics
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: catholics_ddp += 6*(1-dissent); resources -= 1

We have increased our campaigning among Catholics.
